FloraGUI: disambiguate an optional-parameter overload call
==========================================================

ILSpy renders `FloraGUI.Awake`'s call as a bare `OpenAllFloraPage()`, which C#
cannot resolve because both overloads have all-optional parameters:

    public void OpenAllFloraPage(bool fromBackButton = false)
    public void OpenAllFloraPage(bool immediate = false, bool playSounds = true, bool fromBackButton = false)

The original IL picks the three-argument overload explicitly:

    IL_003a: ldarg.0
    IL_003b: ldc.i4.0
    IL_003c: ldc.i4.1
    IL_003d: ldc.i4.0
    IL_003e: call instance void FloraGUI::OpenAllFloraPage(bool, bool, bool)

so the fix spells the arguments out. Purely a source-level repair; the emitted
call is the same one the original performs.

--- a/FloraGUI.cs
+++ b/FloraGUI.cs
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@
 		inventoryRef = registrationScript.GetGlobalComponent<InventoryManager>(GlobalObject.INVENTORY_MANAGER);
 		dogGutsManagerRef = registrationScript.GetGlobalComponent<DogGutsManager>(GlobalObject.DOG_GUT_MANAGER);
 		SFXOverlord.LockInWorldSFX(LockReason.FLORA_GUI);
-		OpenAllFloraPage();
+		OpenAllFloraPage(immediate: false, playSounds: true, fromBackButton: false);
 	}
 
 	private void Update()
